From cfedbe8d96d369eeee20b8c454b7cf7ba5404006 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 18:15:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] Keep the first critic-blind screen's approval, harness,
 reading and checks

Adds docs/investigations/stance_2026_10/bias_screen/ (150 files, about
1.0 MB) with a README: the first critic-blind screen of decision D-D56
(2) (b), from its criteria to its reading, final, each a copy of the
file at the same path in the screen's session-scratch folder
(scratchpad2/r10round/bias_screen/; run_logs/ is its logs/, as the
repository's .gitignore ignores every directory named logs). Eight CPU
continuations of stance6_r10LTSB_s42 from its 1,048,576 checkpoint to
2,490,368 (175 updates), 4 control and 4 critic_blind_tail3 (the
normalised tail_3 angle, observation 6, set to 0 at the value
network's input only), paired seeds 2101 to 2131:

- criteria.txt (v2, sha256 9c490cc6..., APPROVED's criteria_sha256),
  APPROVED (7bf25afd..., written at 06:00:05 UTC, 14 s before the
  launch), SCREEN.json and its template, and the builder's
  SHA256SUMS.txt; NOTES.txt and NOTES_criteria.txt, the build's and
  the criteria's notes;
- tools/: the six pinned tools (run_bs.py gzipped) with their five test
  files and two helpers;
- review/: the independent review of criteria v1 and the scorer's v1
  (9 findings, none blocking) and the fixer's record; scratch/: the
  criteria's design notes and checks;
- runs/<name>/ (run_meta.json and check.json), run_logs/ (decided.tsv:
  all 8 COUNTED; the empty crash ledger; the runner's log) and reads/
  (each continuation's markers.txt and m5.txt, and the parent's);
- score/: score_bs 1.1, run once at 09:03:04 UTC: STATUS final; line 1,
  "NOT INFORMATIVE: THE CONTROL ARM DID NOT REPRODUCE THE EARLY RISE OF
  THE ON-POLICY TAIL_3 COMMAND (...); no reading about the critic is
  made": the control median +0.06027, a rise of +0.09184 against the
  pre-registered 0.10; report only, p 13/70;
- check/stat/ and check/proc/: the two independent checks of the
  reading (both agree, no blocking finding; one wording correction,
  STAT-1).

Every copy is byte-identical to its source, absolute session-scratch
paths included, but for two existing kinds of change. redact: 5 workflow
run ids (one distinct), each after the word "workflow", in
NOTES_criteria.txt, review/FIXES.txt, review/NOTES.txt and
review/fixer/criteria_v1_to_v2.diff (2); criteria.txt keeps the one
workflow run id of its line 4, since its sha256 is the approved pin (as
ecs_results/criteria.txt keeps its own). gzip: tools/run_bs.py, which
reads policy_loading's _ensure_sb3 (test_policy_loading.py parses every
Python file under docs/); gunzip restores it, and then sha256sum -c
--ignore-missing SHA256SUMS.txt gives 15 files OK (its other 7 entries
are the validations, not kept) and the six tools equal APPROVED's
tool_sha256. Every source's sha256 equals its entry in the SHA256SUMS of
the screen's durable copy (claude/handoff-bias-screen at cfed2c70, read
in its local clone). Not copied: the sealed code copy (code/, 1,407
files); each continuation's checkpoints, ledger, training episodes,
policy probe, arm evidence per rollout and other run records; the reads'
JSON (their .txt renderings are kept) and the reader's cache; the
validations; the pre-fix and pre-edit copies and a synthetic dry-run
root; the temporary files; the runner's lock file and its process-table
snapshots (proctable.log, which lists the container's own processes).
The durable branch holds all of these that are text but the code copy,
the training episodes, the validations' ledgers, the temporary files and
the empty lock file. 5 files with lines ending in spaces are kept as
their sources have them; the README names them. The Python scripts parse
on Python 3.11, 3.12 and 3.13.

SOURCES.txt gains the note and 150 rows; SHA256SUMS now pins 1678
files (sha256sum -c: all OK); the folder's README gains the entry, the
folder's note under "What changed in the copies", the README among the
files SHA256SUMS does not pin, and four re-check rows; this change's
status row names the folder.

Records only: no library code, configuration, test, notebook, digest or
generated file changes.

