+    <BS>/code -> 331fe8fc..., 1,406 files, equal_to_pinned true, exit 0; no __pycache__ in <BS>/code or <BS>/tools;
+    files newer than <BS>/NOTES.txt outside <BS>: none of mine (only the harness's /tmp logs); <BS> 240 MB; free
+    2,674,622,464 bytes.  <BS>/tmp/pytest_score and pytest_all removed.
+
+==================================================================================================================
+DECISIONS AND WHY (for the reviewer)
+==================================================================================================================
+D1 Primary: the on-policy mean (recommended) rather than the statue_settled 8-row trailing mean: the markers carry it for
+   every row; the verified probe's supported source is on the on-policy rows; 65,536 states per row instead of 2.
+   Its cost: it mixes policy change with state-distribution change (stated in KNOWN LIMITS; statue_settled report only).
+D2 Statistic: the difference of means (the usual exact permutation test); ranks would give the same p floor (1/70).
+   Exact rationals of the recorded doubles (no tolerance): reproducible and well defined; step 7 shows the one way a
+   decimal reading of the data could differ.
+D3 Fill at +-infinity: the only fill that never helps for an unbounded continuous outcome (the supremum of p).  Its
+   consequence, written in the text: one MISSING continuation makes REDUCED unreadable (p >= 36/70).  A reviewer may
+   prefer a bounded fill; any finite fill can help relative to some completion.
+D4 Informativeness 0.10 from B_S (43% of the parent's rise), on the median of the control primaries read; inclusive.
+   B_S is a constant (one start), from the parent's own probe rows ending at S (the continuations' probes hold the
+   same seeded rows, but the markers carry only rows in (S, T)).
+D5 4 + 4 (template), paired seeds, interleaved; the ninth slot unused (a third wave for little power).
+D6 Scorer pin via APPROVED's extra key + criteria PINS + run_meta.approved_sha256, not via bs_common.TOOL_FILES
+   (which would change bs_common.py and require V1 again).  The runner never runs the scorer, so it need not check it.
+D7 Manipulation: CHECK's per-rollout evidence (already built and validated by SCAF) decides VOID; the scorer adds a
+   refusal of markers whose critic form / blind effective slope disagree with the arm, and prints each run's
+   evidence summary.
+
+==================================================================================================================
+OPEN ITEMS
+==================================================================================================================
+O1 Independent review of criteria.txt, score_bs.py and its tests.  ANY change to score_bs.py, test_score_bs.py or
+   SCREEN.json changes their lines in criteria.txt PINS and SHA256SUMS.txt (both must be refreshed; the scorer reports
+   PROVISIONAL while criteria.txt does not name its sha256).
+O2 APPROVED is not written.  After the review the coordinator writes it as criteria.txt "HOW THE COORDINATOR PINS" says
+   (tool_sha256 with the five tools AND "score_bs.py"), then runs run_bs.py --preflight-only for one entry (expected
+   exit 0) and run_waves_bs.sh --plan, and launches per SCAF HOW TO LAUNCH step 5.
+O3 The cited early_bias/NOTES.txt and verify_early_bias/NOTES.txt do not exist; the criteria cite eb_summary.txt,
+   eb_realized.txt, vb_aggregate.txt, vb_realized.txt and RUNLOG 03:45 / 04:21 UTC.
+O4 Two scaffold test files were edited (step 16; not among the five tools; assertions unchanged); the builder's
+   SHA256SUMS.txt is kept as WORK/SHA256SUMS.builder_0500Z.txt.
+O5 [inferred] items in the text a reviewer may want to check: STOPPED only at 2,359,296 (from the ECS text's patience
+   reading); pairing makes the unpaired test conservative if pairs correlate positively; power assumes a normal model
+   and sigma 0.04-0.10 from another phase.
+O6 Disk: 2,674,622,464 bytes free at 05:27 UTC against the runner's launch floor 2,082,471,936; 8 continuations add about
+   0.3-0.4 GB; other workflows share the disk.
+O7 WORK/dryrun_root (about 0.5 MB) is a synthetic root used only for the dry run; it can be deleted.
