+SHA256SUMS.txt -> 22 OK; no <BS>/APPROVED, no <BS>/runs.  Copies of the files before my edits: review/fixer/orig/.
+
+==================================================================================================================
+FINDINGS (each checked against the files; verdict, evidence, change)
+==================================================================================================================
+R1 should-fix (gate and test share the control values) -- FIXED.
+   Verified with my own simulation, written independently of review/rv_sim.py (another seed; 60,000 draws per cell;
+   the test as the observed split's position among the 70 sums), review/fixer/fx_sim.py -> fx_sim.out:
+     P(REDUCED | gate passed) under no effect: true rise 0.10: 0.079-0.084; 0.12: 0.052-0.064; 0.15: 0.043-0.051;
+     0.20: 0.043-0.044; 0.231: 0.042-0.043; P(REDUCED) overall 0.040-0.043 in every cell (<= 3/70 within MC error).
+   The reviewer's figures reproduce.  Change: criteria.txt KNOWN LIMITS, a new item with the reviewer's text (values
+   as computed; "A REDUCED read with a control rise below about 0.15 is less secure than its p says").  No tool change.
+
+R2 should-fix (line-3 text overstates what a null rules out) -- FIXED.
+   Verified: score_bs.LINE_TEXT[3] said "not tested: a reduction smaller than about half the rise"; criteria.txt
+   l178-180 and l291-292 the same.  WORK/power_bs.out: P(REDUCED) at 0.10 is 0.32-0.91 (SD 0.10-0.04).  fx_sim.out:
+   at exactly half the parent's rise (0.1156) 0.38-0.96 independent, 0.29-0.64 with a pair effect of SD 0.06; at 0.10,
+   SD 0.06: 0.62 -> 0.38 with the pair effect (= rv_sim (3b)).
+   Changes:
+   - score_bs.py LINE_TEXT[3] and criteria.txt THE READING line 3, word for word: "(not excluded: a reduction of
+     about half the rise or smaller (power about 0.3-0.9 at half the rise, by the between-continuation spread; lower if
+     paired seeds correlate), other inputs that carry the angle, the phase after E, the rail)"; the text adds "A null is
+     not evidence that the critic plays no part (KNOWN LIMITS, power)".
+   - KNOWN LIMITS Power: the figures assume independent continuations; positive pair correlation lowers them (0.62 ->
+     0.38); "A null therefore does not exclude a reduction of about half the rise ... nor any smaller one".
+   - THE TEST, pairing paragraph: pair correlation makes the unpaired test conservative AND lowers its power (size
+     0.044 -> 0.017, power 0.62 -> 0.38 at SD 0.06 / pair SD 0.06) [computed].
+   - Optional parts, both taken: (a) the scorer prints each arm's sample SD of the primaries read beside mean and
+     median, report only (score.json arm_sd_report_only); criteria "Every line prints" names it. (b) the line-3
